    "created_at": "2015-09-12T04:53:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-12T04:53:15Z",
    "body": "> Maybe it would be best to let the shadow DOM spec maintain the list of disallowed elements for now, and when there is general agreement we can add it back in to HTML?\n\nDefinitely seems like that would be the less costly and time-consuming option. And as far as tracking it, it’s not like it would ever fall between the cracks or anything. Experience in seeing how other cases have been handled in the past seems to suggest it will just naturally bubble up again as a priority after things are further along implementation-wise.\n",
